-off or transition rights; liability caps and indemnities.\n\n**Naming dependencies:** Fund name, ticker, and prospectus references tied to the index trademark; marketing, exchange listing, and website usage; what must change, and how quickly, if the licence lapses.\n\n**Affiliated-information issues:** Whether the index provider or calculation agent is affiliated with the adviser, sponsor, or distributor; overlap between index governance and adviser personnel; data-sharing and confidentiality; related-party fees; conflict disclosures and board oversight under the 1940 Act.\n\n**Contingency diligence:** Identify candidate substitute indices and test their methodology, tracking, and liquidity; assess the prospectus and shareholder-approval implications of a change; establish board escalation triggers.\n\nSubstitution is not guaranteed; counsel should confirm the actual terms.","ttft_ms":3575,"type":"result","duration_ms":5543,"uuid":"cbe37efe-3b4c-4da9-b99f-996e3034f5bf","ttft_stream_ms":412,"time_to_request_ms":68,"first_content_frame_ms":412,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
